# The build context is content/ and nothing else: the Dockerfile stages one jar out of it.
# The README, the compose example and .env.example live in this directory for the reader, not
# for the daemon. The Dockerfile and this file are still sent to the builder - docker needs
# them to run the build - they just cannot be COPYd into an image.
*
!content/
